{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves","id":1016544,"title":"What're some creative ways a dreamspeaker could fight vampires/werewolves?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T07:41:59-08:00","id":1016544,"title":"What're some creative ways a dreamspeaker could fight vampires/werewolves?","content":"Let's say I have life, spirit, matter, prime and forces, what're some creative ways I could use to fight night-folk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:36:22-08:00","id":1016574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves#post1016544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say I have life, spirit, matter, prime and forces, what're some creative ways I could use to fight night-folk?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Welllll.<br /> It really depends on the sphere levels. Let's presume 2-3. And just some random (run-of-the-mill and not-so-standard) stuff:<br /> <br /> Basics:<br /> Life 3 + Matter 2 = Cause direct aggravated damage on vampires<br /> Life 3 + Spirit 2 = Cause direct aggravated damage on shifters<br /> Prime 2 + Forces 3 = FIREBALL. Always a classic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Creativity:<br /> Life 3 + Matter 3 = Turn a vampire into a statue!<br /> Life 3 + Matter 3 + Spirit 2 = Turn a Werewolf into one!<br /> <br /> Alternatively just shapeshift them.<br /> <br /> Forces 3 = Ever wondered what happens if somebody has no friction, because all the friction gets turned into sound? You get a nightfolk cursing loudly while they continue to slide forward until disappearing on the horizon. Accompanied by a lovely high pitched sound. If they had a running start before the effect kicks in, you won't witness it for long.<br /> BONUS: Cliffs.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 + Matter 3 = ACME Anvils. ACME Anvils everywhere. Hey, you said creative.<br /> <br /> Forces 3 + Matter 2 = Turn a shifter's motion into silver. Yes. &quot;Turn their motion into silver&quot;. Don't try to imagine it.<br /> Forces 3 = Turn their sound into added motion. Bonus if they are raging. Is it time for the Mage's trollface yet?<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course then your Mage gets an arrow to the knee and bleeds to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-13-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:24:49-08:00","id":1016627,"title":"","content":"Matter 3/Forces 3 = turn a good measure of earth into Fire = falling while burning until slamming into the ground.<br /> Matter 3 = turn the earth into liquid mud. Wait until they are partially submerged and turn the mud into iron.<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 + Forces 4 = Bend gravity to pull sideways towards a Breach in the Gauntlet. Most Vampires are SOL in the Spiritworld.<br /> <br /> Life 3/Forces 3 = lock a Forcefield unto you that converts incoming blows into fire while protecting you from fire and heal you at the same time (lots of successes)<br /> <br /> Spirit 2/Prime 2/Forces 3= announce a bounty of 20 quint with greatly amplified voice in the Umbra.<br /> Then turn invisible(Forces 2) turn your scent and sound into speed (Matter 3/Forces3) and run away.<br /> <br /> (Pretty much all your spheres)<br /> Ambush(or use an existing fighting place) a Vampire and a Garou in any order you like and alter the evidence and place a convincing trail that points to the other splat. Mind your own business and lay low until the vendetta is over. If necessary pour some oil into the fire (figuratively speaking).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:48:15-08:00","id":1016751,"title":"","content":"Mind 2+ + Anything = Anger issues. Serious ones. The rating isn't precise as far as I remember, though I would make it 3. Turn the Beast or Rage into weapons against the target. You can separate the Thing from the target and turn it into an independent spirit, you can convert Rage Points into Napalm in the mouth of the Garou, you can use Prime to make any frenzy roll into one Agg damage through a deconstruction of the targets Pattern, you can even turn fury in an equal amount of fear or love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:53:23-08:00","id":1016921,"title":"","content":"What you need to keep in mind though, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12664\" data-vbnamecard=\"12664\">KingJohn</a>, in regards of our little listings here..<br /> <br /> ..they are not considering paradigm! These are just 'These spheres can do that'. Purely going by the by-the-book- writeup of the spheres.<br /> <br /> But the most important ting to consider when RPing your Mage is<br /> <br /> '<i>Concerning the spheres, what has my character been taught ICly?<br /> What is my character's belief system?<br /> How do they think magick works?<br /> What have they been taught by the elders, and among those teachings, is there anything that can even be used for combat?</i>'<br /> <br /> Remember that rarely any Mage actually ICly thinks of spheres. They are mostly a Hermetic thing in their Ars, and are being used as a form of Mage Esperanto.<br /> But your Dreamweaver is probably a shaman, thinks in shamanic teachings...and shamatic teachings rarely let you toss a fireball, change forces into matter, or turn invisible on the spot. Mage is a game of, as a player, limiting your character's abilities to their paradigm despite the spheres on paper allowing all sorts of things. The sphere writeups are all-encompassing and paradigm-neutral. The whole shebang the paradigms grab pieces of.<br /> <br /> Your Dreamweaver is probably highly dependant on spirits for their daily magickal work..and using spirits versus, say, shifters, can be problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-14-2016, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T03:36:13-08:00","id":1016971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1016921#post1016921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Dreamweaver is probably highly dependant on spirits for their daily magickal work..and using spirits versus, say, shifters, can be problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>To either party.<br /> It's complicated to determine which being has more pull on spirits, but consider what happens if you manage to ban a spirit aiding the werewolf from doing just that?<br /> <br /> I imagine you'll have trouble communing with the spirits more closely working with the shifters if you're being antagonistic to them.<br /> Also please don't ever mess with roaches near the wolves you're more likely to find in the city...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T04:16:17-08:00","id":1016977,"title":"","content":"So, what are some things I could realistically use as a dreamspeaker (following a paradigm consistent with the tradition) with spirit sphere that would allow me an advantage over the night folk? Any fetishes/rotes? Plus, what's stopping me from utilizing spirit allies against them? Why wouldn't that be ideal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:48:35-08:00","id":1017009,"title":"","content":"Vampires have tremendous difficulty handling the umbral stuff, so what you can do from there has a couple layers of security in your favor.<br /> Shifters are combative powerhouses with spiritual guidance and anger issues, but are even more reliant on it than vampires are shut off it.<br /> <br /> If you thicken the gauntlet, for example, most of what they can do covertly will be much harder.<br /> If you bargain favor with powerful spirits, werewolves can't quite ignore that too.<br /> <br /> What applies to normal people mostly applies here too! <b>What can you already do as a dreamspeaker?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:06:38-08:00","id":1017013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1016977#post1016977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what are some things I could realistically use as a dreamspeaker (following a paradigm consistent with the tradition) with spirit sphere that would allow me an advantage over the night folk? Any fetishes/rotes? Plus, what's stopping me from utilizing spirit allies against them? Why wouldn't that be ideal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which spirits you have and what tribe they come from.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about Werewolf spirits then certain broods will have strong ties with particular tribes of werewolves. For example Rat's brood are almost always favourable to Bone Gnawers. This would lead to a lot of diplomatic tension if you ask certain spirits to go against those they consider allies. Additionally, certain spirits are just unwilling or outright incapable of fighting werewolves due to their shared status as Warriors of Gaia.<br /> <br /> That's not to say all spirits and Garou get on like old buddies. If your character is aware of these politics and is able to exploit them, then it should be possible to get a lot of mileage out of your spirit friends, but then you're going to have to do a heck of a lot to prove yourself more worthy of respect than the Garou.<br /> <br /> However, you can bypass all the politics with Spirit 4 and just force them to do your bidding, but that may cause more problems than it solves. For one, spirits hate this, and will certainly find a way to get revenge or avenge their kind. For another, this kind of behaviour is exactly the kind of crap that makes mages so detested in the Garou community. If they catch a whiff of you doing this, prepare to become a target for their rage.<br /> <br /> Alternative to the Gaian spirits, you can try manipulating or fraternising with the trinity spirits, but this has it's own drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Weaver spirits aren't too fond of mystic mages, preferring technomancers, but ultimately disliking mages in general since they tend to screw around with reality, distorting their webs.<br /> <br /> Wyld spirits are a lot more neutral, but much harder to predict or control. They have a tendency to go off and do their own thing, and prolonged exposure can lead to bouts of Quiet.<br /> <br /> Wyrm spirits are best avoided lest you really want to piss the werewolves off. Plus, you may get a lot of malfean interest. But if you really want to hit them where it hurts, commanding the hordes of corruption personified can be just the ticket.<br /> <br /> Additionally there are naturae, spirits of nature. These guys are more Verbena flavoured, but Dreamspeakers are just as likely to heed their favours. They tend to be more self serving than the Totem spirits above, but that usually means they're unaligned and therefor easier to have them help. Make sure they like you though, they tend to be wary of mages who disregard their domains.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, however, are epiphlings, spirits of concepts like &quot;love&quot; &quot;childhood&quot; &quot;boredom&quot; &quot;the colour orange&quot;. Garou are usually clueless when it comes to these guys, so that can give you a bit of an edge.<br /> <br /> Then there's the chimera, dream spirits which only the Stargazers would really spend much time with, depending on whether your Dreamspeaker has much to do with the Maya or not, these weird beings can provide a whole host of psychological advantage.<br /> <br /> And that's just the middle umbra. Depending on the specifics of your paradigm you could also commune with archetypical spirits of the astral realm such as the Elements, Old Gods like Odin or Zeus's courts, the pantheon of angles, the kingdom of demons, anthropomorphic personifications like the horsemen of the apocalypse or the court of muses.<br /> Pretty much anything that humans have ever thought up or believed. Though it may be much more difficult for a Dreamspeaker to commune with these spirits unless they align with some mythology that they hold in their paradigm.<br /> <br /> Lastly, without going into deep space anyway, there are wraiths. If necromancy is your thing. I don't think I have to tell you the risks involved with making friends on the other side, especially when the shadows take over, but the right set of arcanoi under the right circumstances can be very nice indeed.<br /> <br /> The upside of these High and Low Umbral denizens is that they hold no allegiance to the Garou and the Garou have no real understanding of them. But the politics of both realms are fiendishly complex, while you may get through to some wraith via their fetters, seeking patronage with the archetypes or aid from the stereotypes in the Astral realm can be confounding, and sometimes outright arbitrary. They may take an instant dislike to you simply because you wear blue, or have not enough beard, it really depends on who you try to commune with.<br /> <br /> Beware making deals with demons for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> If that's not enough for you, space has even more creatures, though finding them and striking a deal can quickly become an epic undertaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:23:21-08:00","id":1017025,"title":"","content":"Hammering the 'Like' on what Saikou said.<br /> <br /> But also ultimately the gist is: Dreamspeakers rarely stand a chance if Werewolves suddenly kick in your door.<br /> All the things Saikou listed need preparation and nurturing of the shaman's relations with specific spirits - which, mind you, is a good thing to do for the Shaman in the first place - and might take weeks, months or years. A Shaman can only gain respect among spirits along such lines.<br /> <br /> But still, without doing that the Shaman won't get spirits watching over them, nor will have them on speed dial, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:28:14-08:00","id":1017027,"title":"","content":"I'm not much of an authority on Werewolves at all so I'll stick to the vampires. Befriending a Sun Spirit of whatever type/mythos fits your Shamman belief will pretty much end them. You can even go so far as allowing it to possess you where you will gain its charms, though loose access to spheres temporarily. If you are able to create a Fetish (spirit 4) it would not be to difficult to get a sun spirit to agree to entering one if the destruction of vampires was to be the purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:36:20-08:00","id":1017032,"title":"","content":"Could Life, Spirit (Prime?) be used to block shapeshifting? Or revert them to homid or lupus (would this be Coincidental?)<br /> Prime and Spirit to drain Gnosis? Though without Correspondence to do it from afar, it doesn't seem to be a good idea. Maybe use those Spheres to gift Gnosis, and befriend Garou? You shouldn't be fighting them as a Dreamspeaker :&gt;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:45:29-08:00","id":1017036,"title":"","content":"Life 4, Spirit 2 prevents them from shifting, it would require Life 5 to shift them to another form. I'm not sure if they would get to resist this with ther Gnosis or not but if used against players or major NPCs you might want to think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:32:14-08:00","id":1017053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017013#post1017013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on which spirits you have and what tribe they come from.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about Werewolf spirits then certain broods will have strong ties with particular tribes of werewolves. For example Rat's brood are almost always favourable to Bone Gnawers. This would lead to a lot of diplomatic tension if you ask certain spirits to go against those they consider allies. Additionally, certain spirits are just unwilling or outright incapable of fighting werewolves due to their shared status as Warriors of Gaia.<br /> <br /> That's not to say all spirits and Garou get on like old buddies. If your character is aware of these politics and is able to exploit them, then it should be possible to get a lot of mileage out of your spirit friends, but then you're going to have to do a heck of a lot to prove yourself more worthy of respect than the Garou.<br /> <br /> However, you can bypass all the politics with Spirit 4 and just force them to do your bidding, but that may cause more problems than it solves. For one, spirits hate this, and will certainly find a way to get revenge or avenge their kind. For another, this kind of behaviour is exactly the kind of crap that makes mages so detested in the Garou community. If they catch a whiff of you doing this, prepare to become a target for their rage.<br /> <br /> Alternative to the Gaian spirits, you can try manipulating or fraternising with the trinity spirits, but this has it's own drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Weaver spirits aren't too fond of mystic mages, preferring technomancers, but ultimately disliking mages in general since they tend to screw around with reality, distorting their webs.<br /> <br /> Wyld spirits are a lot more neutral, but much harder to predict or control. They have a tendency to go off and do their own thing, and prolonged exposure can lead to bouts of Quiet.<br /> <br /> Wyrm spirits are best avoided lest you really want to piss the werewolves off. Plus, you may get a lot of malfean interest. But if you really want to hit them where it hurts, commanding the hordes of corruption personified can be just the ticket.<br /> <br /> Additionally there are naturae, spirits of nature. These guys are more Verbena flavoured, but Dreamspeakers are just as likely to heed their favours. They tend to be more self serving than the Totem spirits above, but that usually means they're unaligned and therefor easier to have them help. Make sure they like you though, they tend to be wary of mages who disregard their domains.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, however, are epiphlings, spirits of concepts like &quot;love&quot; &quot;childhood&quot; &quot;boredom&quot; &quot;the colour orange&quot;. Garou are usually clueless when it comes to these guys, so that can give you a bit of an edge.<br /> <br /> Then there's the chimera, dream spirits which only the Stargazers would really spend much time with, depending on whether your Dreamspeaker has much to do with the Maya or not, these weird beings can provide a whole host of psychological advantage.<br /> <br /> And that's just the middle umbra. Depending on the specifics of your paradigm you could also commune with archetypical spirits of the astral realm such as the Elements, Old Gods like Odin or Zeus's courts, the pantheon of angles, the kingdom of demons, anthropomorphic personifications like the horsemen of the apocalypse or the court of muses.<br /> Pretty much anything that humans have ever thought up or believed. Though it may be much more difficult for a Dreamspeaker to commune with these spirits unless they align with some mythology that they hold in their paradigm.<br /> <br /> Lastly, without going into deep space anyway, there are wraiths. If necromancy is your thing. I don't think I have to tell you the risks involved with making friends on the other side, especially when the shadows take over, but the right set of arcanoi under the right circumstances can be very nice indeed.<br /> <br /> The upside of these High and Low Umbral denizens is that they hold no allegiance to the Garou and the Garou have no real understanding of them. But the politics of both realms are fiendishly complex, while you may get through to some wraith via their fetters, seeking patronage with the archetypes or aid from the stereotypes in the Astral realm can be confounding, and sometimes outright arbitrary. They may take an instant dislike to you simply because you wear blue, or have not enough beard, it really depends on who you try to commune with.<br /> <br /> Beware making deals with demons for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> If that's not enough for you, space has even more creatures, though finding them and striking a deal can quickly become an epic undertaking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, does axis mundi (or any other list) contain these archetypal spirits? I know Axis Mundi has moon spirits (such as the Harvester and the Blood Warrior, the latter of which is absolutely awesome) but I'm not sure about sun spirits, angels, greek/nordic spirits, etc. Where can I check into that? Where can I check into ephlingings, too? <br /> <br /> Are there any haitian/african based/mexican/mayan based (tribal based, essentially) spirits? Also, from what I understand, the main source of strength for a dreamspeaker is probably rotes and or fetishes. Is there a place where I can retrieve a list of fetishes or rotes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:04:55-08:00","id":1017068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017053#post1017053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, does axis mundi (or any other list) contain these archetypal spirits? I know Axis Mundi has moon spirits (such as the Harvester and the Blood Warrior, the latter of which is absolutely awesome) but I'm not sure about sun spirits, angels, greek/nordic spirits, etc. Where can I check into that? Where can I check into ephlingings, too?<br /> <br /> Are there any haitian/african based/mexican/mayan based (tribal based, essentially) spirits? Also, from what I understand, the main source of strength for a dreamspeaker is probably rotes and or fetishes. Is there a place where I can retrieve a list of fetishes or rotes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Axis Mundi is mostly Totem spirits and Naturae, but it does have a few Epiphlings in there. Mage 2nd ed, Book of mirrors, and Book of Worlds have a handful of other epiphlings and archetypical spirits that can be used as templates. Infinite Tapestry probably has the most in regards to spirits resident to the Astral Realm though. Other than that, you'd have to wait until they release the M20 Gods and Monsters book. Going back to WTA, Rage Across the Heavens has a lot of information of planet celestines, including Hellios the Sun God, and can serve as inspiration for concoting your own.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are a number of spirits which are based on Hatian or Myan spirits, but personally I'm not too familiar with these cosmologies, so I can't think of any right now. That being said, nothing says you can do a bit of research yourself, discuss your findings with the ST, and talk about how they may include these pantheons in your game. Make spirits stats is actually really easy.<br /> <br /> Think about how revered they are and give them an Essence rating to match that ( 20 is weak, 40 is normal, 60 is strong, 80 is formidable, and anything about 100 is very powerful, any higher than that and you're dealing with being you most definitely shouldn't be.)<br /> <br /> The rest are just a scale of 1-10.<br /> <br /> Willpower: how meticulous, accurate, and agile are they?<br /> Rage, how &quot;warrior&quot; are they?<br /> Gnosis, how insightful and wise are they?<br /> <br /> Then think about what these mythical beings are capable of in their mythology, and pick a few charms to suit (or make up your own).<br /> <br /> For example. Let's take Zeus.<br /> <br /> He's not really all that revered these days, and has lost a lot of his god status. but he's still an important figure in peoples imagination, so he's likely to be around Essence 75<br /> <br /> The guy used to be the king of gods, and was known for both his wrath as well as his greatness. So arguably he'd have a good Willpower (perhaps 6) and a lot of Rage (either 8 or 9). However, there are numerous stories of Zeus being tricked or fooled by those lesser than him, and many versions of the Greek Mythology portray him as a fairly selfish and selfimportant character. So he'd probably have a low Gnosis (Let's say about 4).<br /> <br /> So this incarnation of Zeus would be Rage 9, Gnosis 4, Willpower 6, Essence 75.<br /> <br /> Charm wise, he'd have to have &quot;Lightning Bolts&quot;.<br /> He'd also have Materialise and Shapeshif, since there are several stories of Zeus transforming into animals an messing around with mortals in disguise.<br /> You get the idea. So dive in to your mythologies, take a look at some Werewolf spirits for comparison, and have fun with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Fetishes. These are just items which have spirits residing within. If you befriend a spirit and agree to a deal, it may inhabit an object for you to call on it when needed. Spirits will not do this lightly, however, and may be quite particular about what they will be happy to enter.<br /> Again Spirit 4 bypasses these problems by forcing them inside an object, but that's no way to make friends.<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers also get access to Totems, which work similarly to WTA totems, but aren't limited to Gaia broods. You can see a list of stuff like this in the Dreamspeakers Tradition Guide.<br /> <br /> If you want a list of fetishes, then you're best bet would be the WTA books, though they are really Werewolf specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:10:04-08:00","id":1017128,"title":"","content":"Spirit Ways has rules regarding spirit allies, as well as a few examples (spirit crow, black dog making for a nice combination).<br /> Fire is strongly connected with shamanism and fire and fire spirits work against pretty everyone more or less.<br /> Familiars can get really powerful (the bad luck charm in FbDF is way OP IMHO)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:11:26-08:00","id":1017129,"title":"","content":"Ya know, Spirit really comes down to not being the best sphere to use against WW. Intead use Life 4, Matter 2, Spirit 2 and change their blood to silver and be done with it.<br /> <br /> Used after a Matter 3 effect to solidify the air and immobolize them there wont be much to worry about. Of course you'll need to make the effects fit your paradigm. But they could easily be explained as curses which should fit Dreamspeaker beliefs. Remember that even if you belive that its through spirits that your magick manifests if Sphere wise your not useing/manipulating spirits then you technically aren't. And even if your ST rules against that idea they still aren't spirits in the since that they would be aginst you and sell you out to the wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:19:34-08:00","id":1017167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017129#post1017129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya know, Spirit really comes down to not being the best sphere to use against WW. Intead use Life 4, Matter 2, Spirit 2 and change their blood to silver and be done with it.<br /> <br /> Used after a Matter 3 effect to solidify the air and immobolize them there wont be much to worry about. Of course you'll need to make the effects fit your paradigm. But they could easily be explained as curses which should fit Dreamspeaker beliefs. Remember that even if you belive that its through spirits that your magick manifests if Sphere wise your not useing/manipulating spirits then you technically aren't. And even if your ST rules against that idea they still aren't spirits in the since that they would be aginst you and sell you out to the wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to do what a shaman realistically could against these creatures...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:28:42-08:00","id":1017175,"title":"","content":"Nothing I suggested is any more or less realistic to what a shamman could do than anything else presented. Especially when represented as a curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:12:05-08:00","id":1017251,"title":"","content":"hmm the 'blood to silver' curse idea isn't bad actually. since the werewolf curse is spirit oriented you just need to flavor your magic as calling on it's spiritual bane to justify the spell. How Do You Do That basically says 'add spirit 2' to any spell if you feel you'd be calling on spiritual power. so basically you'd be calling on it's own curse against it as vengeance for striking out at you as a shaman (assuming you think it's okay to do that, if you offended it you may want to try something else). as to the vamp, anything involving fire/sunlight should make it run like heck","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:15:28-08:00","id":1017256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017068#post1017068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Axis Mundi is mostly Totem spirits and Naturae, but it does have a few Epiphlings in there. Mage 2nd ed, Book of mirrors, and Book of Worlds have a handful of other epiphlings and archetypical spirits that can be used as templates. Infinite Tapestry probably has the most in regards to spirits resident to the Astral Realm though. Other than that, you'd have to wait until they release the M20 Gods and Monsters book. Going back to WTA, Rage Across the Heavens has a lot of information of planet celestines, including Hellios the Sun God, and can serve as inspiration for concoting your own.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are a number of spirits which are based on Hatian or Myan spirits, but personally I'm not too familiar with these cosmologies, so I can't think of any right now. That being said, nothing says you can do a bit of research yourself, discuss your findings with the ST, and talk about how they may include these pantheons in your game. Make spirits stats is actually really easy.<br /> <br /> Think about how revered they are and give them an Essence rating to match that ( 20 is weak, 40 is normal, 60 is strong, 80 is formidable, and anything about 100 is very powerful, any higher than that and you're dealing with being you most definitely shouldn't be.)<br /> <br /> The rest are just a scale of 1-10.<br /> <br /> Willpower: how meticulous, accurate, and agile are they?<br /> Rage, how &quot;warrior&quot; are they?<br /> Gnosis, how insightful and wise are they?<br /> <br /> Then think about what these mythical beings are capable of in their mythology, and pick a few charms to suit (or make up your own).<br /> <br /> For example. Let's take Zeus.<br /> <br /> He's not really all that revered these days, and has lost a lot of his god status. but he's still an important figure in peoples imagination, so he's likely to be around Essence 75<br /> <br /> The guy used to be the king of gods, and was known for both his wrath as well as his greatness. So arguably he'd have a good Willpower (perhaps 6) and a lot of Rage (either 8 or 9). However, there are numerous stories of Zeus being tricked or fooled by those lesser than him, and many versions of the Greek Mythology portray him as a fairly selfish and selfimportant character. So he'd probably have a low Gnosis (Let's say about 4).<br /> <br /> So this incarnation of Zeus would be Rage 9, Gnosis 4, Willpower 6, Essence 75.<br /> <br /> Charm wise, he'd have to have &quot;Lightning Bolts&quot;.<br /> He'd also have Materialise and Shapeshif, since there are several stories of Zeus transforming into animals an messing around with mortals in disguise.<br /> You get the idea. So dive in to your mythologies, take a look at some Werewolf spirits for comparison, and have fun with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Fetishes. These are just items which have spirits residing within. If you befriend a spirit and agree to a deal, it may inhabit an object for you to call on it when needed. Spirits will not do this lightly, however, and may be quite particular about what they will be happy to enter.<br /> Again Spirit 4 bypasses these problems by forcing them inside an object, but that's no way to make friends.<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers also get access to Totems, which work similarly to WTA totems, but aren't limited to Gaia broods. You can see a list of stuff like this in the Dreamspeakers Tradition Guide.<br /> <br /> If you want a list of fetishes, then you're best bet would be the WTA books, though they are really Werewolf specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't get access to the books you mentioned, mind listing some ephlingings/their stats?<br /> <br /> Sun/fire spirit really interest me, but Axis Mundi doesn't seem to contain those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:31:54-08:00","id":1017269,"title":"","content":"I think you want Mage's Book of worlds. it paints a very different view of the umbra than the werewolves. the conflict between gaia and the triat is muted and the umbra is instead a realm of myths. it's still the same place but the mages go much farther afield (if not quite so deeply into any one place). the umbra is presented as a realm where every god could and does exist. a dreamspeaker might be limited by this as they subscribe to roughly the same paradigm as the garou but another mage would be more than capable of calling forth a guardian angel, an jann, or a warrior ghost from the higher and lower umbra who care nothing for gaia's war. it's interesting because it can really bring in how mages only see what they believe to be true, in fact essence can change the input your getting, and it could actually lead to an angels versus starships possibililty were the celestial chorus to majorly engage the technocracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 12-14-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:37:57-08:00","id":1017276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017269#post1017269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you want Mage's Book of worlds. it paints a very different view of the umbra than the werewolves. the conflict between gaia and the triat is muted and the umbra is instead a realm of myths. it's still the same place but the mages go much farther afield (if not quite so deeply into any one place). the umbra is presented as a realm where every god could and does exist. a dreamspeaker might be limited by this as they subscribe to roughly the same paradigm as the garou but another mage would be more than capable of calling forth a guardian angel, an jann, or a warrior ghost from the higher and lower umbra who care nothing for gaia's war. it's interesting because it can really bring in how mages only see what they believe to be true, in fact essence can change the input your getting, and it could actually lead to an angels versus starships possibililty were the celestial chorus to majorly engage the technocracy</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there specific beings (like specific angels, jann/ghosts) that I need to know about that have pre-set stats and everything, or can I do research and make them myself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:43:52-08:00","id":1017287,"title":"","content":"You don't need the Spirit sphere or actual spirits <i>per se</i>. A shaman have this as Paradigms, which mostly means to believe in magic as coming from the spirits of things.<br /> <br /> That said, you can, let's say, use Matter, Entropy, Correspondence and Forces to commune with the spirit of a gun, present it to a doll of your target, and ask the spirit to find your target by happenstance, aim to the head by happenstance, and &quot;accidentally&quot; shoot pure silver. Ask the spirits of gunpowder and silver to deliver the gun the strength for the task. And wait. Eventually the gun will arrive and deliver, going from hand to hand, by accident, as gift, and every happenstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:45:14-08:00","id":1017289,"title":"","content":"alien horrors of various kinds, dream spirits, a few epiphlings, a minor angel, the archangel gabriel, pattern and chaos spirits, typhon, some weird animal things, dinosaur spirits, autocthonian spirits and etherships are all given stats in chapter 6","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:48:44-08:00","id":1017292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017256#post1017256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't get access to the books you mentioned, mind listing some ephlingings/their stats?<br /> <br /> Sun/fire spirit really interest me, but Axis Mundi doesn't seem to contain those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 150 of Axis Mundi will give you a few Epipihlings<br /> <br /> Here's a couple from Book of Worlds<br /> <br /> Akai, love Epiphlings<br /> Appears as a shimmer of light. represents love in all its forms from familiar to sexual, parental to platonic.<br /> R 3<br /> G 10<br /> W 3<br /> E 30<br /> Charms: Airt Sense, Appear, Cleanse the Bligh, Influence, Shapeshit.<br /> <br /> Loors, Colour Epiphlings<br /> Floating forms of raw colour, be it floating blobs of paint, wispy clouds of hue, or a simply change of shaded light. They acommunicate visually and abstractly, and tend to change colour and texture depending on their mood.<br /> R 3/6<br /> G 6<br /> W 4<br /> E 15-25<br /> Charms: Airt Sense, Illuminate, Influence, Shapeshift<br /> <br /> Shanti, Peace Epiphlings<br /> Healing winds, rather rare these days. They somtimes take the form of waves, rainbow hued clouds, or symbols like doves or olive trees.<br /> R 0<br /> G 8<br /> W 5<br /> E 20<br /> Charms: Airt Sense, Cleanse the Blight, Influence.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are a few more in this book, with much more detailed descriptions, but I'm not sure what Onyx Path would say about a full transcript of their material onto their forums. That might be going into the realm of Copyright Infringement.<br /> <br /> This is a PDF of all spirits recorded across the World of Darkness as of 2001 along with the books they were sourced from, a list of published Epiphlings appears from the top of page 5<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.pen-paper.net/wp-content/themes/magazine-basic/library/images/404.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Pen &amp; Paper News </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> However, I think they intend that you use these spirits as frameworks or an inspiration to build from. It's not that hard, just take a feeling that you've experienced and try to imagine what it might do, or say, or think if this feeling was its own entity with self-awareness. Then attach some stats to it in a logical way.<br /> <br /> As for the Sun spirit Helios. He's a celestine, so you're going to have to do quite a lot of work to gain his attention, let alone his favour.<br /> Celestines don't tend to have stats since they are so powerful they can just do whatever they want. In WTA cosmology, celestines literally are the things they represent. i.e. Helios is literally the Sun, and Luna the Moon. If either of those spirits disappear in WTA, so do their mundane counterparts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-14-2016, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:50:50-08:00","id":1017294,"title":"","content":"For the most part you and your ST will need to create specific spirits as the one presented are fairly basic, but there are plenty examples to mimic. For a sun spirit just take any fire spirit, replace &quot;fire&quot; with &quot; solar flare&quot; and you are pretty much done for powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:06:15-08:00","id":1017302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017292#post1017292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 150 of Axis Mundi will give you a few Epipihlings<br /> <br /> Here's a couple from Book of Worlds<br /> <br /> Akai, love Epiphlings<br /> Appears as a shimmer of light. represents love in all its forms from familiar to sexual, parental to platonic.<br /> R 3<br /> G 10<br /> W 3<br /> E 30<br /> Charms: Airt Sense, Appear, Cleanse the Bligh, Influence, Shapeshit.<br /> <br /> Loors, Colour Epiphlings<br /> Floating forms of raw colour, be it floating blobs of paint, wispy clouds of hue, or a simply change of shaded light. They acommunicate visually and abstractly, and tend to change colour and texture depending on their mood.<br /> R 3/6<br /> G 6<br /> W 4<br /> E 15-25<br /> Charms: Airt Sense, Illuminate, Influence, Shapeshift<br /> <br /> Shanti, Peace Epiphlings<br /> Healing winds, rather rare these days. They somtimes take the form of waves, rainbow hued clouds, or symbols like doves or olive trees.<br /> R 0<br /> G 8<br /> W 5<br /> E 20<br /> Charms: Airt Sense, Cleanse the Blight, Influence.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are a few more in this book, with much more detailed descriptions, but I'm not sure what Onyx Path would say about a full transcript of their material onto their forums. That might be going into the realm of Copyright Infringement.<br /> <br /> This is a PDF of all spirits recorded across the World of Darkness as of 2001 along with the books they were sourced from, a list of published Epiphlings appears from the top of page 5<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.pen-paper.net/wp-content/themes/magazine-basic/library/images/404.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Pen &amp; Paper News </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> However, I think they intend that you use these spirits as frameworks or an inspiration to build from. It's not that hard, just take a feeling that you've experienced and try to imagine what it might do, or say, or think if this feeling was its own entity with self-awareness. Then attach some stats to it in a logical way.<br /> <br /> As for the Sun spirit Helios. He's a celestine, so you're going to have to do quite a lot of work to gain his attention, let alone his favour.<br /> Celestines don't tend to have stats since they are so powerful they can just do whatever they want. In WTA cosmology, celestines literally are the things they represent. i.e. Helios is literally the Sun, and Luna the Moon. If either of those spirits disappear in WTA, so do their mundane counterparts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't Zeus be a celestine, too? Because you said earlier I'd be able to make an incarnation of Zeus as a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:14:09-08:00","id":1017308,"title":"","content":"that's just be up to you using the normal spirit rules. you could argue that he's a celestine of great power who embodies storms and lordship.... or you could say he's an obsolete storm spirit who's power has faded. or you could go both ways and say that the presented stats are for an avatar of zeus. mage is flexible like that (sometimes in annoying ways)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:21:40-08:00","id":1017313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017302#post1017302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But wouldn't Zeus be a celestine, too? Because you said earlier I'd be able to make an incarnation of Zeus as a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the WTA and MTA cosmologies start to clash.<br /> <br /> In WTA, Celestines are the single most powerful beings in the world. Most Werewolfs will only ever meet with Incarna, and even then they'd be lucky. These spirits are the reason the mundane world exists in the first place. They hold reality together and as such as immeasurably powerful. Their abilities are independent of what the mundane world know of them, because these beings already are the mundane world, whether the people like it or not.<br /> <br /> In MTA, Gods exist as spirits because enough people believe they exist. There is debate over which came first, but a gods power seems to be intimately tied to human perception. Because practically no one believes in Zeus these days, he's been demoted from god status, to more of an Archetype status. Anyone familiar with Greek mythology will be aware of who Zeus was, even if it's just through the Disney movie, but no one reveres him the same way that people do the god of the Abrahamic religions or the Hindu deities today.<br /> <br /> Whether you want to say that WTA is correct, and all other gods are simply really intricate Epiphlings created by Humans, denizens to the Astral Realm or the Mythical Realm, or say that MTA is correct, and the only reason Celestines are so powerful is because so many Garou serve them and believe in them, to the point of enforcing the very cosmology they describe, it's up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:44:17-08:00","id":1017624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017313#post1017313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is where the WTA and MTA cosmologies start to clash.<br /> <br /> In WTA, Celestines are the single most powerful beings in the world. Most Werewolfs will only ever meet with Incarna, and even then they'd be lucky. These spirits are the reason the mundane world exists in the first place. They hold reality together and as such as immeasurably powerful. Their abilities are independent of what the mundane world know of them, because these beings already are the mundane world, whether the people like it or not.<br /> <br /> In MTA, Gods exist as spirits because enough people believe they exist. There is debate over which came first, but a gods power seems to be intimately tied to human perception. Because practically no one believes in Zeus these days, he's been demoted from god status, to more of an Archetype status. Anyone familiar with Greek mythology will be aware of who Zeus was, even if it's just through the Disney movie, but no one reveres him the same way that people do the god of the Abrahamic religions or the Hindu deities today.<br /> <br /> Whether you want to say that WTA is correct, and all other gods are simply really intricate Epiphlings created by Humans, denizens to the Astral Realm or the Mythical Realm, or say that MTA is correct, and the only reason Celestines are so powerful is because so many Garou serve them and believe in them, to the point of enforcing the very cosmology they describe, it's up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are there lists of elemental spirits (like rock spirits, fire spirits, water spirits etc) that a dreamspeaker can summon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:55:46-08:00","id":1017629,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure M20 has that in the back of the book under antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T16:58:30-08:00","id":1017858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017624#post1017624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are there lists of elemental spirits (like rock spirits, fire spirits, water spirits etc) that a dreamspeaker can summon?</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 has a long list of elementals at the back, that's correct. You'll find them from page 636.<br /> <br /> There are also a list of elementals in Axis Mundi from page 132.<br /> <br /> M20 has almost all of the elementals listed in Axis Mundi, except for the Plastic Elemental. But Axis Mundi goes into far more detail about these elementals than M20 does. You'll find the Ice elemental in Axis Mundi under Wendigo's Brood, but no Storm or Wood elemental, at least as far as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there are the Bane elementals, which can be found either in WTA or in Book of the Wyrm. But as stated above, it's really unlikely a Dreamspeaker would try to gain their company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T17:08:38-08:00","id":1017861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1017858#post1017858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 has a long list of elementals at the back, that's correct. You'll find them from page 636.<br /> <br /> There are also a list of elementals in Axis Mundi from page 132.<br /> <br /> M20 has almost all of the elementals listed in Axis Mundi, except for the Plastic Elemental. But Axis Mundi goes into far more detail about these elementals than M20 does. You'll find the Ice elemental in Axis Mundi under Wendigo's Brood, but no Storm or Wood elemental, at least as far as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there are the Bane elementals, which can be found either in WTA or in Book of the Wyrm. But as stated above, it's really unlikely a Dreamspeaker would try to gain their company.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wanted to crystalize a vampire's internal organs/make them catch on fire, or make their body constrict around a certain area (that would kill them) what spheres would I need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T17:18:58-08:00","id":1017867,"title":"","content":"Life 4, Matter 2, possibly Forces 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T12:23:32-08:00","id":1018172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1016627#post1016627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matter 3/Forces 3 = turn a good measure of earth into Fire = falling while burning until slamming into the ground.<br /> Matter 3 = turn the earth into liquid mud. Wait until they are partially submerged and turn the mud into iron.<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 + Forces 4 = Bend gravity to pull sideways towards a Breach in the Gauntlet. Most Vampires are SOL in the Spiritworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Life 3/Forces 3 = lock a Forcefield unto you that converts incoming blows into fire while protecting you from fire and heal you at the same time (lots of successes)</b><br /> <br /> Spirit 2/Prime 2/Forces 3= announce a bounty of 20 quint with greatly amplified voice in the Umbra.<br /> Then turn invisible(Forces 2) turn your scent and sound into speed (Matter 3/Forces3) and run away.<br /> <br /> (Pretty much all your spheres)<br /> Ambush(or use an existing fighting place) a Vampire and a Garou in any order you like and alter the evidence and place a convincing trail that points to the other splat. Mind your own business and lay low until the vendetta is over. If necessary pour some oil into the fire (figuratively speaking).</div> </div> </div> </div>For the one in bold, would I erect such a forcefield in a ritual and use it as protection whenever my mage is out?<br /> <br /> As for the umbra, how do I forcefully sidestep a vampire or a werewolf into the umbra? Because as far as I understand, once they're in the umbra I can mold their patterns like clay and make them dissipate into mist (with spirit 3)<br /> <br /> Also would a vampire be blocked from using their abilities in the umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T13:50:14-08:00","id":1018212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018172#post1018172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for the umbra, how do I forcefully sidestep a vampire or a werewolf into the umbra? Because as far as I understand, once they're in the umbra I can mold their patterns like clay and make them dissipate into mist (with spirit 3)<br /> <br /> Also would a vampire be blocked from using their abilities in the umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being more familiar with Werewolf and Vampire than Mage, the answers I have are going to be less relevant.<br /> <br /> That being said, you can force them into the Umbra using Spirit (4 I think) to tear a hole in the Gauntlet, but that doesn't convert them to Ephemera. Meaning you would still need the normally required Spheres (Life/Matter or Life/Spirit) to affect them. The Spirit Sphere alone will not let you &quot;mold their patterns like clay&quot; if they are in the Umbra. They are still composite beings.<br /> <br /> In one of the editions (not sure M20 treats it), the book went with the idea that Spirit 3 could move the Mage to the Umbra, but converted them to spirit matter in doing so. Even under that assumption, Werewolves for sure would still be able to do anything and everything they normally could and would come out as composite creatures since that's just kind of what they are.<br /> <br /> Vampires should likewise remain composite creatures (unless specifically converted to Ephemera) but wouldn't have access to creatures with blood, so they wouldn't be able to feed to replenish their blood pools (there are some rare exceptions to this). And since most don't have a way to escape the Umbra, you could just leave them there and wait for them to fall into torpor in a couple of weeks or get incinerated by the Umbral sun.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, but yes, the Vampire's abilities would be block, sort of. They would be limited to affecting things in the Umbra. This is a general thing, there are some exceptions (like always).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-16-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:00:45-08:00","id":1018216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018212#post1018212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being more familiar with Werewolf and Vampire than Mage, the answers I have are going to be less relevant.<br /> <br /> That being said, you can force them into the Umbra using Spirit (4 I think) to tear a hole in the Gauntlet, but that doesn't convert them to Ephemera. Meaning you would still need the normally required Spheres (Life/Matter or Life/Spirit) to affect them. The Spirit Sphere alone will not let you &quot;mold their patterns like clay&quot; if they are in the Umbra. They are still composite beings.<br /> <br /> In one of the editions (not sure M20 treats it), the book went with the idea that Spirit 3 could move the Mage to the Umbra, but converted them to spirit matter in doing so. Even under that assumption, Werewolves for sure would still be able to do anything and everything they normally could and would come out as composite creatures since that's just kind of what they are.<br /> <br /> Vampires should likewise remain composite creatures (unless specifically converted to Ephemera) but wouldn't have access to creatures with blood, so they wouldn't be able to feed to replenish their blood pools (there are some rare exceptions to this). And since most don't have a way to escape the Umbra, you could just leave them there and wait for them to fall into torpor in a couple of weeks or get incinerated by the Umbral sun.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, but yes, the Vampire's abilities would be block, sort of. They would be limited to affecting things in the Umbra. This is a general thing, there are some exceptions (like always).</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'd have to specifically convert them to ephmera? So for a vampire I'd have to use life + matter + spirit to convert them to ephmera, and life + spirit to convert a werewolf to ephmera and send them into the umbra at the same time?<br /> <br /> How would I imprison a werewolf/fera in the umbra, since some can travel back and forth between the umbra?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T14:19:29-08:00","id":1018223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018216#post1018216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I'd have to specifically convert them to ephmera? So for a vampire I'd have to use life + matter + spirit to convert them to ephmera, and life + spirit to convert a werewolf to ephmera and send them into the umbra at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be my call on it. Something that's ephemera only needs the Spirit Sphere to affect it. For Vampires the effect/Spheres make sense. The Spheres for the Garou also makes sense, but you aren't so much converting them to ephemera as removing the Life component from them (they are already half ephemera). The end result is the same though. As pure Spirits it is also completely arguable that they'd have trouble coming back to the Material.<br /> And again, edition matters here. Depending on edition you may or may not have to split successes. M20 does away with splitting successes but allows Nightfolk to roll countermagic (sometimes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018216#post1018216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How would I imprison a werewolf/fera in the umbra, since some can travel back and forth between the umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way is to just raise the Gauntlet. You could also throw in Correspondence to ward the area or to teleport them someplace else in the Umbra. They will likely find their way back, but that takes time and for the sake of the scene would accomplish your goal.<br /> <br /> Edit: and again, exceptions exist to all of this but it seems unhelpful to discuss those exceptions, even though ST can go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:46:58-08:00","id":1018241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018172#post1018172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the one in bold, would I erect such a forcefield in a ritual and use it as protection whenever my mage is out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is a possibility.<br /> Anotherway would be to hang the effect with Time 4 until needed.<br /> Or crafting a charm with Prime 2/3<br /> <br /> Another protection method is the fetish \u201cCloe the growl-growl bear\u201c (FbDF) a protective mother-bear spirit that can manifest as a bear, deal with umbral attackers and she can also heal you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:51:04-08:00","id":1018243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018241#post1018241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that is a possibility.<br /> Anotherway would be to hang the effect with Time 4 until needed.<br /> Or crafting a charm with Prime 2/3<br /> <br /> Another protection method is the fetish \u201cCloe the growl-growl bear\u201c (FbDF) a protective mother-bear spirit that can manifest as a bear, deal with umbral attackers and she can also heal you.</div> </div> </div> </div>She can also deal with other attackers, too, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:53:11-08:00","id":1018245,"title":"","content":"Yes, she manifests as a big bear for attackers on this side of the gauntlet. For umbral attackers she can stay in spirit form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T22:25:34-08:00","id":1018347,"title":"","content":"Cloe is a classic protection, but also a relatively simple (if somewhat powerful) Fetishe. You can try other spirits for other effects, or even make a collection of such items. It seems quite in-character for most shamans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T14:43:21-08:00","id":1018591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1018245#post1018245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, she manifests as a big bear for attackers on this side of the gauntlet. For umbral attackers she can stay in spirit form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I read about Cloe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T22:25:28-08:00","id":1018694,"title":"","content":"Forged by Dragon's Fire, the Revised-Era source-book on Wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T01:01:59-08:00","id":1356018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1016751#post1016751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 2+ + Anything = Anger issues. Serious ones. The rating isn't precise as far as I remember, though I would make it 3. Turn the Beast or Rage into weapons against the target. You can separate the Thing from the target and turn it into an independent spirit, you can convert Rage Points into Napalm in the mouth of the Garou, you can use Prime to make any frenzy roll into one Agg damage through a deconstruction of the targets Pattern, you can even turn fury in an equal amount of fear or love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-visiting this thread, I wanted clarification on this.<br /> <br /> What is 'rage points into napalm&quot; mean? And the Thing is, I assume, how they shift?<br /> <br /> And isn't mind 2 only suggestion? Wouldn't mind 3 be needed for actual anger issues?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T01:29:14-08:00","id":1356022,"title":"","content":"Also, given Werewolves's high soaking dice, is it even possible for a spirit mage to touch them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T05:12:05-08:00","id":1356046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1356018#post1356018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And isn't mind 2 only suggestion? Wouldn't mind 3 be needed for actual anger issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind 2 it's also for instilling/reducing emotions<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is 'rage points into napalm&quot; mean? </div> </div> </div>Don't know for sure, but I assume it's to use Forces 3 to transmute the psychic energy into fire. Which would both reduce it and damage the werewolf (which would increase it afterwards, so I'm not sure how efficient would this be. I'm inclined to say &quot;not much&quot;, but these things can vary).<br /> <br /> I don't think Mind/Forces alone should work to transmute Rage because it has a strong spiritual aspect (I would add Spirit 3).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Thing is, I assume, how they shift? </div> </div> </div>I think it refers to the Beast/Rage (was mentioned in the previous sentence).<br /> <br /> One would need to use Spirit 5 to do that, perhaps coupled with equally great levels of Mind and some Prime<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, given Werewolves's high soaking dice, is it even possible for a spirit mage to touch them? </div> </div> </div>Yes, to touch them you can use your hands. It's Spirit 2 if they're on the Penumbra. Keeping your hands (or life) after doing that it's not guaranteed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Damaging them may be harder, though. It depends on the nature and characteristics of the attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-20-2019, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T05:35:47-08:00","id":1356063,"title":"","content":"There are some really <i>nasty </i>ideas in this thread, like that &quot;Blood into Silver&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I would rule it as Matter 3/Life 3/Spirit 3 direct attack, not possible to dodge, that causes the standard successes*2 levels of Aggravated of Life attacks, but with the qualities of silver (usually can't be soaked). Add Forces to make it molten hot silver and it does ( successes + 1) *2 of Aggravated Silver levels of damage.<br /> <br /> Would that count as &quot;touching&quot; a werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-20-2019, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T19:37:54-08:00","id":1356220,"title":"","content":"They could get the trees to grapple and stake a vampire. Werewolves would be trickier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T20:56:48-08:00","id":1356579,"title":"","content":"I'd be tempted to do something nonlethal but distracting, like call up the spirits of all the fleas and chiggers in the region and sic them on the werewolves. Maybe Mind 2 Spirit 2 to cause significant penalties to dicepools while they're scratching uncontrollably?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Oh, but yes, the Vampire's abilities would be block, sort of. They would be limited to affecting things in the Umbra. This is a general thing, there are some exceptions (like always). </div> </div> </div>A problem with that is I think a lot of vampires' mental powers could still work on physical beings able to perceive them through the Gauntlet. So the people waiting nearby for the 9pm bus to Downtown would be protected by their inability to make eye contact or be entranced by the vampires' faces, but your Dreamspeaker wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T04:35:16-08:00","id":1356615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves?p=1356579#post1356579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem with that is I think a lot of vampires' mental powers could still work on physical beings able to perceive them through the Gauntlet. So the people waiting nearby for the 9pm bus to Downtown would be protected by their inability to make eye contact or be entranced by the vampires' faces, but your Dreamspeaker wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires can't see naturally through the Gauntlet (neither can mages), though. I think *they* may be unable to make eye contact w/o Thaum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T12:30:32-08:00","id":1356676,"title":"","content":"I thought from the other side of it in the penumbra the physical world was still visible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T03:31:48-08:00","id":1357015,"title":"","content":"Nope. Some stuff may have a reflection on the other side, but Werewolf has rules about seeing the real world from the Penumbra (and how doing so prevents them from seeing the Umbra at the same time, barring Gifts), and Mage seems to follow the same assumptions here<br /> <br /> Note that Werewolves have innate powers to see through the Gauntlet, mages and vampires don't.<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands, on the other hand, do seem to allow to see the physical world from the other side","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-26-2019, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T13:26:43-08:00","id":1360374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016544-what-re-some-creative-ways-a-dreamspeaker-could-fight-vampires-werewolves#post1016544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say I have life, spirit, matter, prime and forces, what're some creative ways I could use to fight night-folk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets make it as simple and coincidental as possible.<br /> Spirit: Easy talens of sun, fire, or silver spirits. <br /> Matter: Add to life and spirit to charge werewolf blood with silver particles. add to life to turn vampire hearts into wood. <br /> Life: add spirit/matter to fuse joints.<br /> Forces: launch and direct silver or wooden needles right to hearts. <br /> <br /> really depends on the cituatuation and exact opponent tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}